tion>Spivak AC, Sanderman J, Bowen JL, Canuel EA, Hopkinson CS. Global-change controls on soil-carbon accumulation and loss in coastal vegetated ecosystems. Nat. Geosci. 2019;12:685&#x2013;692. doi: 10.1038/s41561-019-0435-2.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41561-019-0435-2</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Kirwan ML, Megonigal JP. Tidal wetland stability in the face of human impacts and sea-level rise. Nature. 2013;504:53&#x2013;60. doi: 10.1038/nature12856.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nature12856</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24305148</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Duarte CM, Losada IJ, Hendriks IE, Mazarrasa I, Marba N. The role of coastal plant communities for climate change mitigation and adaptation. Nat. Clim. Chang. 2013;3:961&#x2013;968. doi: 10.1038/nclimate1970.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/nclimate1970</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rogers K, et al. Wetland carbon storage controlled by millennial-scale variation in relative sea-level rise. Nature. 2019;567:91&#x2013;95. doi: 10.1038/s41586-019-0951-7.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41586-019-0951-7</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30842636</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Megonigal JP, Schlesinger WH. Enhanced CH4 emissions from a wetland soil exposed to elevated CO2. Biogeochemistry. 1997;37:77&#x2013;88. doi: 10.1023/A:1005738102545.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1023/A:1005738102545</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Beaulieu JJ, DelSontro T, Downing JA. Eutrophication will increase methane emissions from lakes and impoundments during the 21st century. Nat. Commun. 2019;10:3&#x2013;7. doi: 10.1038/s41467-019-09100-5.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1038/s41467-019-09100-5</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">